  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kommuri Ananda Rao vs The State Of Ap on 1 October, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5895 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "1. In this Criminal Petition, filed under Section 482 of Cr.P.C., the Petitioner/Accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.109 of 2019 of Cherukupalli Police Station, Guntur district, which was registered for the offences under Sections 188, 272, 273 and 420 IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short, 'the FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the Petitioner/Accused, briefly, are that on 13.06.2019 at 10:00 a.m., when the complainant along with his staff proceeded to Khadar Khan Center, Cherukupalli village and mandal, found the petitioner, who is in possession of Gutka and tobacco products, having purchased the same to sell in his shop at higher price, and on interrogation as the accused voluntarily confessed to have been engaged in the business of prohibited tobacco products, seized the same, registered F.I.R., remanded him to judicial custody for the offences stated supra.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
